+// interval to read the port's rp_cnp_handled. A dead peer's CQE comes only after the retry limit, about a minute,
+// but every retransmission to its gone QP raises the counter within tens of ms. A live peer whose QP failed raises
+// it too, so a ring neighbour is dead only if its socket (collComm keeps one to each, unused after setup) is closed
+// while packets sent to it are not acknowledged.
